  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1802.05 Diadromous",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1802.05 “Diadromous” means regularly migrating between freshwater and salt water. This category includes anadromous, catadromous, and amphidromous fish such as sea-lampreys, sturgeons, salmons, and alewives. Migration should be cyclical and predictable.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1800) #8326, eff 4-21-05; ss by #9330, eff 11-26-08; ss by #12185, eff 5-25-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1800.html"
